 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d choose an indoor workout in Jurong right now**, especially if you planned to run or do anything strenuous. As of **8:00 a.m. Saturday, October 17**, the latest West Singapore reading I could find was **109 µg/m³ for 1-hour PM₂.₅—“Elevated”**—and a **24-hour PSI of 179, “Unhealthy.”** Jurong is in the West reporting region. ([haze.sg](https://www.haze.sg/))\n\nFor a healthy adult, **a short, easy walk is a more reasonable choice than a hard workout**. Singapore’s NEA advises reducing strenuous outdoor activity when 1-hour PM₂.₅ is Elevated; children, pregnant people, older adults, and people with heart or lung disease should avoid strenuous outdoor activity. NEA also advises avoiding prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion when planning activities today. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nCheck the **West 1-hour PM₂.₅ reading in myENV or NEA’s haze site immediately before heading out**—it can change from hour to hour. It’s also currently showing a shower in the Jurong area, so don’t exercise outside if you hear thunder. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
